    "title": "Course record stands test of time at the Augusta National",
    "text": "NEWSCourse record stands test of time at the Augusta NationalJohn Boyettejohn.boyette@augustachronicle.comApril 9, 2011, 5:55 p.m. ETTwenty-five years ago, Nick Price set the course record at Augusta National Golf Club using a wooden driver and laying up on all the par-5 holes.Technological advances in golf clubs and balls have been great since then, but only Greg Norman has matched Price's 9-under-par 63 at the Masters Tournament.While there have been a handful of 59s in PGA Tour history, 24 times a player has shot 63 in one of golf's four majors. Norman and Vijay Singh are the only ones to do it twice.Already a subscriber? Sign inTwo ways to continue readingPay Annually$119SAVE 50% versus MonthlySubscribeSubscribers getBEST DEALFull access to augustachronicle.com including articles, videos, and moreA subscription to shareAccess to the eNewspaperShow featuresMonthly$1for the first monthSubscribeSubscribers getFull access to augustachronicle.com including articles, videos, and moreA subscription to shareAccess to the eNewspaperShow featuresInterested in other subscriptions? Learn more",
